{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793531499,"nonce":"gtjuyZX+j3D2JA0NqamRCklYVAk=","title":"Found by the ADR-0077 grill audit, 2026-11-01. Code path read; the end-to-end failure is INFERRED (no test covers it).","message":"At Depot replicaCount \u003e 1 with caches on, a REQUIRED input fetch can fail:\n1. The executor adds the cache restore roots to the workspace token's `roots` claim (crates/scarab-executor-k8s/src/lib.rs:524-530).\n2. A blob GET lands on a replica whose BlobAllowlist (replica-local, workspaced.rs:1747) has no entry for the token, so it walks every claimed root (singleflight_walk, ~2002).\n3. A cache root's trees are warm-only and scattered across replicas, so tree_entries_anywhere (~3850) returns NotFound for them.\n4. The incomplete walk is a 500 (workspaced.rs:2125, \"F3: an incomplete walk is a 500\"), in `log` mode too, because the mode is checked only at the deny site.\n5. wsfetch retries 5xx for the whole root (scarab-wsfetch.rs:331); retries re-scatter; the Attempt ends Transient and relaunches with the same hints.\n\nFix (~30 LOC): a cache restore root that cannot be walked is left out of the grant (and the grant does not claim completeness for it) instead of failing the walk; a required input root that cannot be walked keeps today's 500. Test at the functional grain: two Depot routers on one Postgres + bucket, a cache root present on only one, a required-input GET to the other succeeds.\nShips before route-by-cache-key (12e2f6b).","files":null}]}